# ------------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
#
# `.env` holds live Serper, Brave, Firecrawl and Anthropic credentials plus the
# service's own admin keys. It must never reach the repository — the tracked
# templates are `.env.example` and `.env.prod.example`, which carry no values.
#
# `deploy/pre-commit` is a second line of defence; install it with:
#   git config core.hooksPath deploy/githooks
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example

# Certificates and private keys, in case one is ever generated in-tree.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
*.ppk

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- tests
#
# Deliberately NOT pushed — kept on the local machine only.
#
# Consequences to be aware of:
#   - CI cannot run them, so `.github/workflows/ci.yml` verifies only that the image
#     builds and that no credential is committed. Nothing gates correctness.
#   - A clone (including the EC2 box) has no way to self-verify.
#   - They exist in exactly ONE place. There is no second copy anywhere.
#
# Run them locally before every push:
#   python -m pytest tests -q          # expect 502 passed
tests/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- node
# admin-ui carries its own .gitignore too; these cover an invocation from the root.
node_modules/
.next/
.vercel/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- misc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
.nginx-test/
